  ],
  "version": 1,
  "fields": {
    "phrase": "BIP-39's 24-word all-zero-entropy phrase; every epoch key below derives from it (rootKeys + handleRoot).",
    "chainId": "Base Sepolia. The anchor domain also names verifyingContract, a placeholder address (keccak of a fixed string).",
    "keys": "registrar: keccak256(\"cofferdam-handles-0086-fixture:registrar\"); owner and newOwner: the phrase's epoch 0 and 1 handle keys.",
    "epochs": "Per epoch: the handle key address (the anchor owner), the 66-byte meta-address (spending key then viewing key, compressed), the self-derivation seed.",
    "handleIds": "handleId = keccak256(utf8(\"cofferdam-handle-v1:\" + label)), label in its stored ENSIP-15 form.",
    "eip712": "Per domain: the domain, its separator, and per primary type the canonical type string, keccak256 of it (typeHash) and the fields in order.",
    "fieldConventions": "nonce (anchor): the anchor's one per-handle counter of accepted signed calls, read at signing; pendingNonce: the nonce at which the pending change was queued; deadline, frozenUntil, expiresAt: unix seconds; metaAddress: 66 bytes; nonce (registry): 32 random bytes, refused twice before expiresAt.",
    "signed": "One message per primary type: the signing role, its address, the message, the EIP-712 structHash and digest, and the 65-byte signature r||s||v (v 27/28, low s, RFC 6979). Recovering the digest must give signerAddress.",
    "stealth": "ERC-5564 scheme 1: R = r*G (compressed), h = keccak256(compressed r*V), viewTag = h[0], P = S + h*G, signer = address(P), stealthPrivateKey = s_spend + h mod n, account = CREATE2(factory.address, salt = signer left-padded to 32 bytes, factory.initCodeHash). The factory is the never-deployed placeholder until decision 0083 rule 4's exists.",
    "selfDerived": "Self-derived addresses (0086 rule 1): r(p, i) = HKDF-SHA256(selfDerivationSeed, salt \"cofferdam-root-keys-v1\", info utf8(\"self-ephemeral\") || u8 p || u32be i) mod n; then as stealth."
  },
